  "notes": [
    "Static art for dice mini-games: twelve blank dice (six shapes in bone and in slate) and six pip stamps. Nothing here is an animation.",
    "pivot (48, 48) is the centre of each die's result face; draw every die and its markings around it. 'bounds' is the whole visible die, not the result face.",
    "A result is drawn by stamping pips, or a numeral the game supplies, onto the blank die. A pip's 'crop' is its tight source rectangle in the cell; stamp it at native size.",
    "Only the D6 has pip layouts. For the other shapes the guide suggests a numeral inside numeralBox, since their faces have no room for many pips.",
    "Rolling is shown by jiggling the same die for about rollFeedbackMs; there are no tumbling frames."
  ]
